  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Selam Connecting for Culture Africa 2023 -2028</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Selam Connecting for Culture Africa 2023-2028 - Selam 2023-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet &quot;Connect for Culture Africa&quot; &#xe4;r ett fem&#xe5;rigt initiativ som syftar till att &#xf6;ka kultursektorns roll i Afrika. Initiativet mottar finansiellt st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n den regionala sektionen p&#xe5; ambassaden i Addis Abeba. Under Selams ledning ska ett n&#xe4;tverk av kulturf&#xf6;respr&#xe5;kare verka f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;ka beslutsfattares f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else om f&#xf6;rdelarna med investera i kultur. Syftet &#xe4;r att st&#xe4;rka till kulturakt&#xf6;rers m&#xf6;jligheter att p&#xe5;verka och delta i afrikanska l&#xe4;nders budgetprocesser. Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att &#xf6;ka den politiska viljan kring kultursatsningar och att i slut&#xe4;ndan se ett &#xf6;kat budgetanslag till kultur och kreativa sektorer i Afrika. Initiativet ska vidare skapa f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;ttningar f&#xf6;r kultur att fr&#xe4;mja m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter, demokrati, jobbskapande, teknik och digitalisering p&#xe5; kontinenten. Initiativet &#xe4;r regionalt i sin ansats med ett initialt landfokus p&#xe5; de fem k&#xe4;rnl&#xe4;nder. Projektet kommer att utf&#xf6;ras i n&#xe4;ra dialog och samarbete med Afrikanska Unionen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Connect for Culture Africa&quot; project is a five-year initiative that aims to increase the role of the cultural sector in Africa. The initiative receives financial support from the regional section at the Embassy in Addis Ababa. Under Selam&apos;s leadership, a network of cultural actors will work to increase decision-makers&apos; understanding of the benefits of investing in culture. The aim is to strengthen the opportunities for cultural actors to influence and participate in African countries&apos; budget processes. The overall goal is to increase the political will around cultural investments and to ultimately see an increased budget allocation to culture and creative sectors in Africa. The initiative will further create the conditions for culture to promote human rights, democracy, job creation, technology and digitization on the continent. The initiative is regional in its approach with an initial country focus on the five core countries. The project will be carried out in close dialogue and collaboration with the African Union.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &quot;Connect for Culture Africa&quot; is a five-year program that aims to intertwine advocacy efforts at regional and national levels through a network of culture advocates dedicated to raising awareness on the benefits of investing in culture. The objective of the project is to contribute to increased voice among culture actors to influence and participate in budget processes that aim at securing resources to the culture and creative sectors. The project aims at contributing to an increased political will that translates to budget proposals, budget bills, and in increased budget allocation to the culture and creative sectors in Africa. The project focuses on creating conditions for culture to play its potential role in promoting human rights, democracy, job creation, tech and digitisation as well as peace and reconciliation in Africa, with an initial focus on the five core countries Ethiopia, Kenya, Nigeria, South Africa and Morocco.</narrative>
  </description>
